.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt MUSTACHE-ADA 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mustache-ada
.Nd a complete Mustache template engine in Ada
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Bd -literal -offset indent
with Mustache;
.Ed
.Pp
In a GNAT project file the library is selected with
.Ql with "mustache";
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
renders a template \(em text with
.Ql {{...}}
tags \(em against a
.Em view :
a stack of scopes, each a tree of
.Sy Scalar ,
.Sy List
and
.Sy Map
values.
It implements the whole core Mustache spec and passes its official test
suite (136 tests), and it is the engine that turns a grammar's abstract
tree into the target language's syntax, so an emitter never hardcodes a
keyword.
.Sh TAGS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic {{var}}
HTML-escaped interpolation.
.Ql & ,
.Ql < ,
.Ql > ,
.Ql \&"
and
.Ql '
become
.Ql &amp; ,
.Ql &lt; ,
.Ql &gt; ,
.Ql &quot;
and
.Ql &#39; .
.It Ic {{{var}}} , {{&var}}
Raw interpolation, with no escaping.
.It Ic {{#var}} ... {{/var}}
Section: a list iterates, a map is pushed once, a truthy scalar renders
once.
.It Ic {{^var}} ... {{/var}}
Inverted section: renders iff
.Ar var
is falsey
.Pq false, null, the empty string, or an empty list .
.It Ic {{! comment }}
Comment, rendered to nothing.
.It Ic {{>partial}}
Include a partial, with standalone-line indentation.
.It Ic {{=<< >>=}}
Change the delimiters for the rest of the template.
.It Ic {{.}}
The current value, the implicit iterator.
.It Ic a.b.c
Dotted-name lookup through nested maps.
.El
.Pp
A missing name or partial renders empty \(em it is never an error.
.Sh VALUES
A
.Vt Mustache.Value
is a discriminated record in one of three kinds:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy Scalar
A string, built with
.Fn New_Scalar Ar text .
.It Sy List
A list of values, built with
.Fn New_List
and grown with
.Fn Append Ar list Ar item .
.It Sy Map
A set of named values, built with
.Fn New_Map
and grown with
.Fn Insert Ar map Ar key Ar item .
Binding a key already present replaces it.
.El
.Pp
The builders return a
.Vt Mustache.Value_Access
.Pq a pointer to a heap value ,
so a view is a tree the caller drops when done; nothing is deallocated.
.Sh VIEW AND RENDERING
.Fn View
returns a fresh
.Vt Mustache.Context
.Pq a scope stack with one empty map .
.Fn Put Ar view Ar key Ar value
adds a string or a value to the top scope;
.Fn Push
and
.Fn Pop
stack scopes for sections and partials.
.Fn Render Ar source Ar view
renders a template given as a string, and
.Fn Render_File Ar name Ar view
renders a template loaded by name.
.Sh PARTIALS
.Fn Define Ar name Ar source
registers a partial from a string,
.Fn Load Ar dir
reads every
.Pa dir/*.tmpl
.Pq keyed by base name, without the
.Ql .tmpl
suffix ,
.Fn Reset
forgets every registered template, and
.Fn Get Ar name
returns a template's source text.
.Sh ERRORS
.Vt Mustache.Template_Error
is raised only for a template that cannot be parsed: an unterminated tag, a
section with no closing tag, or a bad delimiter change.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
with Mustache;  use Mustache;

V : Context := View;
Put (V, "name", "Ada");

declare
   L : constant Value_Access := New_List;
begin
   Append (L, New_Scalar ("alpha"));
   Append (L, New_Scalar ("beta"));
   Put (V, "items", L);
end;

Put_Line (Render ("Hello {{name}}!", V));
Put_Line (Render ("{{#items}}[{{.}}]{{/items}}", V));
.Ed
.Pp
prints
.Ql Hello Ada!
and
.Ql [alpha][beta] .
